a massive legal settlement will  compensate victims of the Las Vegas  massacre and their families MGM Resorts  will pay up to 800 million dollars  resolving lawsuits across several states  plaintiffs had claimed the hotel  conglomerate failed to protect concert  goers and prevent the shooter from  stockpiling weapons  Mireya Villarreal has reaction from  families who say the agreement will  finally allow them to heal  two years later nothing's changed as far  as good days and bad days  after seven surgeries shrapnel in her  brain a lost eye and what doctors called  a miraculous recovery from legal  blindness 30 year-old single mother  Chelsea Romo is ready to move forward I  have no choice I have two kids I have to  make it work Romo was one of the 22,000  people attending an outdoor Las Vegas  concert on October 1st 2017 when gunman  Steven paddock opened fire on the crowd  from windows of the Mandalay Bay Hotel  58 people died and more than 600 people  like Romo were wounded I have not been  able to go back to where right now I  have no medical insurance I have medical  bills I have a lot that I that I carry  now with my injuries the possible 800  million dollar settlement could impact  the more than 4,000 people currently  seeking damages attorney James France  represents Romo in about 200 other  victims I think it's the right step and  it's the right thing to do to make  restitution and not put the victims  through any more turmoil Romo says she  has more surgeries on the horizon but  knows better days are ahead of her I now  appreciate everything I see everything I  do so much more  MGM International Resorts which owns  Mandalay Bay released a statement that  says we our goal has always been to  resolve these matters or the community  the victims and their families can now  move forward we know that judges and  attorneys will now be working together  to figure out how  we'll divide this settlement money  between the more than 4,000 possible  victims involved Tony  Maria thank you
 

